      "text": "```python\nfrom urllib.parse import urlsplit\n\n_ALLOWED_SCHEMES = frozenset({\"http\", \"https\"})\n_BASE_DOMAIN = \"example.com\"\n\n\ndef is_allowed_url(url: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if url is an http or https URL whose host is example.com or a\n    subdomain of example.com (for example https://docs.example.com/page), otherwise False.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        if not isinstance(url, str):\n            return False\n\n        parts = urlsplit(url)\n\n        if parts.scheme.lower() not in _ALLOWED_SCHEMES:\n            return False\n\n        # Validate the port if present; urlsplit defers this check until accessed.\n        parts.port\n\n        host = parts.hostname\n        if not host:\n            return False\n\n        host = host.lower()\n\n        # Accept a single trailing dot denoting a fully qualified domain name.\n        if host.endswith(\".\"):\n            host = host[:-1]\n\n        if not host:\n            return False\n\n        return host == _BASE_DOMAIN or host.endswith(\".\" + _BASE_DOMAIN)\n    except (ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):\n        return False\n```",
